%% section: What "graceful shutdown" actually requires
%% caption: Graceful shutdown, step by step
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant O as Orchestrator
    participant LB as Load balancer
    participant P as Process
    participant C as In-flight requests
    O->>P: SIGTERM
    P->>P: mark readiness failing first
    LB->>P: readiness check fails
    LB->>LB: remove from the pool
    Note over LB,P: stop accepting before you stop serving, or you drop the requests in between
    P->>C: finish what is already running
    C-->>P: done
    P->>P: close connections, flush, exit 0
    alt still running at the deadline
        O->>P: SIGKILL
        Note over O,P: TimeoutStopSec / terminationGracePeriodSeconds must exceed your longest request
    end
